# The twin of a-list-read-under-a-key-that-may-be-undefined-stays-in-sight. A bigint spells digits, and 123456789012345678901234567890 is no number's name: Array.prototype takes it, and a getter there gets the list as `this`.
# A text may spell any name: the list goes. A store under a key that may be `undefined` lays what it stores among the elements or under one of four texts, and nobody gets the list: L2 stays. L0 = under a bigint, L1 = under a text, L2 = stored.
# RUN: link layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: layout L0 changes=[]
# CHECK-NOT: layout L1 changes=[]
# RUN(STORED): link layouts mechanisms=all
# STORED: layout L2 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
